---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import MediaFigure from "../components/MediaFigure.astro";
---
<Base
  title="Lineage — Gourmet Gastronomer and Sour Flour"
  description="How Gourmet Gastronomer relates to Sour Flour: historical lineage, not a storefront."
  permalink="/sour-flour/"
  crumbs={[{ name: "Lineage", url: "/sour-flour/" }]}
>
  <main class="home" id="main">
    <header class="page-hero">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Lineage</p>
        <h1>Gourmet Gastronomer and Sour Flour</h1>
        <p class="lede">
          This encyclopedia is independent knowledge work. Sour Flour is a later,
          real-world expression of one slice of the same idea.
        </p>
      </div>
      <MediaFigure name="loaf" />
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Gourmet Gastronomer existed as an idea before Sour Flour: learn food
        deeply enough that the world of food becomes more interesting, then
        make that knowledge usable. Sour Flour grew out of the bread portion of
        that project — teaching, baking, and community in San Francisco. It is
        not the parent of this site, and this site is not a Sour Flour catalog.
      </p>
      <p>
        Bread knowledge here lives on canonical pages: the
        <a href="/learn/sourdough/">sourdough pathway</a>,
        <a href="/baking/sourdough/starter/">starters</a>,
        <a href="/baking/sourdough/bulk-fermentation/">fermentation</a>,
        and the teaching
        <a href="/recipes/country-loaf/">country loaf</a>.
        For current classes, bread, or pickup, use Sour Flour’s own site.
        Hours and offers change; we do not mirror them.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/learn/sourdough/">Learn sourdough</a>
        {" · "}
        <a href="/recipes/country-loaf/">Country loaf</a>
        {" · "}
        <a href="/about/">About this encyclopedia</a>
        {" · "}
        <a href="https://sourflour.org/">sourflour.org</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
</Base>
